# count-hardened.log: the gate-count baseline for 5.9 and 5.11.
#
# The spike's gate-count crate (`spikes/s5-recair/count` on branch
# `spike/s5-recair` at a2784b49) re-run on vos-core at 15f98b6e, the hardened
# segment AIR: 25 chips, format 31's inner parameters (blowup 4, 44 queries,
# PoW 20, interaction PoW 8, FRI fold step 1, last layer degree 1). Ported in
# a scratch worktree, not committed:
# - the chips are the AIR's 25, in `chip_idx` order; the window kernel's shape
#   is mask 0x01f9ffff (23 chips, every one but POPCOUNT and BITCOUNT) and the
#   full shape 0x01ffffff;
# - the log sizes are the window kernel's classes 1 (2^15 steps, 8 pages) and
#   0 (2^12, 8) as derive gave them in 5.8.0's window run; POPCOUNT and
#   BITCOUNT at their table size, 8;
# - the recursion AIR's components are vos-recair-air's (5.8), not the spike's
#   own bodies, so its `p2` check is not re-run (5.8's `modes` tests are);
# - `drive_chip_oods` reaches BITWISE_AND_BYTE (the spike's 6acdc7df, landed
#   on vos-core in 5.9).
# The gate counts do not depend on the log sizes; the leaf, fold and wrap
# models do. Counts [measured], rows [model], memory and time [projected], as
# `recursion-air.md` tags them.
# Run on the Intel Core Ultra 7 155H, release build, load average 3–5.

